DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261013T150000
DTSTAMP:20261014T045844Z
UID:28803db08de33f32b2bec7af6381@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Make clay beads honoring each living wild bison in North Ameri
 ca with artist Cannupa Hanska Luger for Census - Bison Bead Project. As pa
 rt of the For Freedoms residency with the National Gallery of Art and the 
 Corcoran School of the Arts & Design\, visiting artist Cannupa Hanska Luge
 r invites the D.C. community to make beads representing over 500\,000 livi
 ng bison in the form of 36 life-size sculptures. The Bison Bead Project st
 ems from Luger’s Counting Coup social engagement series\, which engages 
 collective making to build large-scale collaborations that lend humanity t
 o abstract data and connect us in the process. Corcoran students are hosti
 ng bead making workshops to help contribute to this\nCategory: Arts & Cult
 ure\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/census-bison-bead-pr
 oject
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/census-bison-bead-project
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
