CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:In a region with a history of commodity shocks and debt crises
 \, why has China maintained financial ties with many economically risky co
 untries in the Americas? Why does China explicitly criticize austerity and
  policy conditionality\, yet implicitly support these same policies throug
 h its IMF partnership? This project develops a theoretical framework for g
 lobal financial statecraft. The traditional approach to sovereign debt sus
 tainability\, led by the IMF and Paris Club\, emphasizes the short-term vi
 ability of sovereign borrowers by promoting financial disclosure and econo
 mic reform. China participates in such multilateral initiatives\, signalin
 g its willingness to be a global stakeholder\, but o\nCategory: Academic\n
 Original listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/chinas-challenge-managing
 -debt-and-development-chinas-financial-statecraft-in-the-americas
