SUMMARY:The 2026 Donald R. Dunner Endowed Lecture — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261027T193000
DTSTAMP:20261014T045844Z
UID:f4ecc5894ba197a28023089ace1f@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures & Speakers\,Washington\, DC\,United St
 ates
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for GW Law’s 2026 Donald R. Dunner Endowed Le
 cture. The lecture will feature contemporary thought-leaders addressing la
 w and practice topics inspired by Don’s legacy. Don made singularly impo
 rtant contributions to the patent profession\, from a seminal role in the 
 creation of the Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit to arguing 175 Fe
 deral Circuit appeals that helped to shape much of modern patent law. His 
 extraordinary contributions to the profession were further evident in his 
 numerous leadership roles within the organized bar and his decades-long te
 aching role at GW Law. Register for the Event Here\nCategory: Lectures & S
 peakers\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/the-2026-donald-
 r-dunner-endowed-lecture
